name ai_source_loss_5pct
describe Two-way audio call (user <-> AI), the AI's replies from #4's example source sent at real time, 5% random loss each way on a 100 ms RTT link (#759)
duration 30s
call two-way
video off
ai_source speed=3x burst=1s gap=300ms first_chunk=400ms
turn user 1s-4s
turn ai after=800ms len=4s
turn user 10s-13s
turn ai after=700ms len=5s
turn user 20s-22s
turn ai after=600ms len=5s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=50ms queue=300ms loss=5%
reverse at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=50ms queue=300ms loss=5%
# program.md 6.3 sev:2, for each direction: no audio interruptions in moderate loss (<= 5%), mouth-to-ear delay
# under 400 ms on a 100 ms RTT link, and no bottleneck queue held over 200 ms. The AI source never falls behind
# real time at 3x (no underruns). Conversation rows: the user hears every reply (sev:1), and at most 2% of the user's
# speech is lost or concealed on the way to the AI (sev:2).
# Target (program.md 6.3 sev:2 conversation): conv.response_delay_p95_ms < 500. Missed today (746-818 ms on seeds 1-5)
# because the metric counts the source's 400 ms first chunk; follow-up #969. No expect line until it is decided; the
# baseline holds today's value.
expect up.audio.interruptions == 0
expect down.audio.interruptions == 0
expect up.audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 400
expect down.audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 400
expect up.cc.queue_over_200ms_pct == 0
expect down.cc.queue_over_200ms_pct == 0
expect ai.turns == 3
expect ai.underruns == 0
expect conv.responses == 3
expect conv.user_speech_lost_pct <= 2
# program.md 6.3 sev:2 conversation: on a 100 ms RTT link the transport adds at most 500 ms to the response; the
# source's first-chunk generation is the AI's own time, not the transport's (Owner, on #3).
expect conv.response_delay_p95_ms < 500
